# Spotlight → System Settings → Spotlight → Results from Apps that should be off.
# Alphabetical by the name shown in that list. 17 apps.
# macconfig does not read the on/off toggles: com.apple.Spotlight
# EnabledPreferenceRules is the list of rows, and a row stays after the
# toggle is turned off. The manual step is check by hand. Nothing is written.
# Format: plain name | bundle id
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.
#
# Leave these on (do not add them here): App Store, Calculator, Dictionary,
# System Settings, WhatsApp.
Books|com.apple.iBooksX
Calendar|com.apple.iCal
Contacts|com.apple.AddressBook
Keynote|com.apple.iWork.Keynote
Mail|com.apple.mail
Messages|com.apple.MobileSMS
Music|com.apple.Music
Notes|com.apple.Notes
Numbers|com.apple.iWork.Numbers
Photos|com.apple.Photos
Podcasts|com.apple.podcasts
Reminders|com.apple.reminders
Safari|com.apple.Safari
Shortcuts|com.apple.shortcuts
Stocks|com.apple.stocks
Tips|com.apple.tips
Voice Memos|com.apple.VoiceMemos
